From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 01:27:49 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_sandbox, settings_ui: Hide the Host on by default;
 Reserve CPUs moves to the page
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two operator decisions of 2026-11-22 on the agent sandbox.

Reserve CPUs was a button beside the thread's lock (0146). The operator
found it out of place there and asked for it in the settings window. It
is now a switch on the Agent Sandbox page, beside a new "Hide the Host"
switch for agent_sandbox.mask_host, which had no switch at all (0146 read
it only for the command preview). agent_jail_host.rs (new) draws both from
host_switches, a pure model: each follows the project's own choice, then
the default; while Hide the Host is on, Reserve CPUs shows on and
disabled, because its CPU files must match the cores the jail runs on
(launch.rs already reserved under mask_host). Both write the project's
entry -- set_project_reserve_cpus (0146) and set_project_mask_host (new,
beside set_project_connectors) -- and apply on the next start. Beside the
lock only "Shares CPUs" stays, as information: render_cpu_shared_label
replaces render_cpu_reservation_toggle.

Hide the Host is on by default. The operator saw a jailed agent read the
machine's CPU model, thread count, RAM and swap, and chose "default, plus
an extra layer" (the extra layer -- mount sources, kernel, load -- is an
ai-jail change of its own). default.json and the settings fallback say
true. --mask-host is the fork's (sys-apps/ai-jail-3.5.0-r2), and 0146
refuses to start a jail that asks for it from an ai-jail without the
option (fail closed), so the ebuild's RDEPEND moves to 3.5.0-r2 and the
refusal and the missing-ai-jail tooltip name that version and the page's
switch. Only a custom ai_jail_path at an older binary meets the refusal.

Tests: agent_jail_host_tests (the model: the default hides and reserves,
a project's own choices replace it); host_view_launch_hides_the_host_by_
default (a settings file that never names mask_host passes --mask-host
and pins). The fixtures that predate the host view (agent_sandbox launch and round
trip, agent_servers sandbox hooks) now set it off,
as they set the limits off for §6.54; the missing-ai-jail tooltip test
reads -r2. Red seen with default.json false and the forced reservation
dropped: both new tests failed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---

